{1900}{497l Last Will and Testament
{1910}{28l Your very soul is blasted!}
{1920}{497l 	If you are reading this, then it is my hope that you are the one I sent for those many weeks ago, but if you are not, I hope you can still feel it in your heart to help me and my people, especially my daughter.
{1921}{497l		For you to understand what is happening here, it will be best for me to tell my tale from the beginning. This village has been a happy one for most of its existence. When our beloved king died, it was his wish that we leave the castle empty, as his monument. And so it was, for years following his demise.
{1922}{497l 	Some time ago, the winds changed, and an unease swept over the town. People began to disappear in the night. All our attempts to thwart whoever was invading our town as we slept came to naught. The local mage, after a fortnight of fasting and meditation, told us that the evil that had come upon us was living deep within our sacred castle. If calmer heads had not prevailed, the whole town would have besieged the castle that night. The first group of volunteers set out to destroy the evil that had come to dwell among us the next morning. They were never heard from again.
{1923}{497l		We have sent several groups since then, with none ever returning. The last of us will be going at first light, and my daughter is meant to be among us, but I cannot allow this. She is too precious to me to see her die. Find her, and keep her safe.
{1924}{497l		Please, help her, help us all.
{1925}{497l	Your friend,				
{1930}{497l		My only hope is that friendly eyes are reading this. I have to chance leaving this in this place, as I fear my time is near. We are preparing for our final assault on the demonic mistress that has brought such terror on our village.
{1931}{497l		Somewhere in the village I once called home you will find a rather tame wolf. This is not a wolf, but in actuality, my daughter. She is under a spell I had the mage cast on her myself, in a misguided attempt to keep her safe. My fear is that she will now be condemned to live out her days in that bestial form. Please use the scroll of dispel magick I have hidden here with this book to return her to her beautiful human form.
{1932}{497l		Please help us. You are our only hope.
{1940}{497l		The mistress has gone insane! I fear for my life every day, and I only do her bidding in a vain attempt to have my meager existence spared from the horrors she is capable of. I am writing this now so that perhaps someone, someday, will know I only helped her out of fear, though I will surely pay for my sins in the world to come. Please, pray for me...
{1941}{497l		The mistress has always been a cruel woman, beating her servants mercilessly, but at least we were being fed and clothed. Besides, most days she was too consumed with her petty delusions to pay us any mind. But that all changed when she beat Ursula mercilessly, and got her blood on her hands. She was then convinced that the spots that had been touched by blood had actually become younger. She felt she had discovered the secret to eternal youth in her servant's blood. She cut out Ursula's heart herself!
{1942}{497l		She began consuming her servants, one by one. I alone was spared, for what reason I do not know. When her servants were gone, she began taking local drunks, and when they were used up, she turned to the young women of the village. We barely escaped that place with our lives.
{1943}{497l		That is when we came to this place. To keep secure from angry villagers, she has sold herself to any number of demonic forces. I pray that I will be forgiven for my part in all this, by whatever powers there may be.}
{1950}{37l Attention miners,}
{1951}{37l Items excavated found on person will be confiscated.}
{1960}{497l  What a tragedy that the two headed calf was born just before she arrived.}
{1961}{497l  How could we have justified turning away an old woman on such a stormy night?  Our foolish superstitions have been our undoing.}
{1962}{497l  If only she had explained that she was a powerfual witch on her way to Tyr for an audience with the queen?  Surely we would have accomodated her.}
{1963}{497l  Instead we turned her away.  But as she left we all heard her cry out.  Cry out the horrible, terrible curse that has decimated Stillglade.}
{1964}{497l  May the gods have mercy upon us.}
{1965}{497l  Leo Lighthold}
{1970}{497l  I have searched and searched but all in vain!  My beloved Drusa lies in my arms, her last breaths escaping even as I pen this and there is naught I can do.}
{1971}{497l  What a wicked, wicked being that old woman is!  To curse us for our ignorance and force us to suffer a cruel and slow death.  I will never forget her mocking words...  "For your inhospitable natures, I place a curse upon you!  Death shall walk your streets and pain be your constant companions for all time!"}
{1972}{497l  We beseached her to undo the curse.  We offered our homes to her then.  But it was too late.  Her heart was cold and hard and she surely mocked us when she ammended her curse by adding "Very well, you piddling fools!  I shall give you this!  Dance upon the waters, deep within the dark.  If perchance you hear a bell, death will leave.  All will be well."}
{1973}{497l  We have tried everything and still we die!  If you read this, I pray, find the answer.  Lift the curse from Stillglade!}
{1974}{497l  John Tarry}
{57100}{28l To carry out the freeing of the soul, the disciple must obtain thread woven by a dark spider. The only way to cut the thread is with a ceremonial dagger whose blade has been dipped in the Fountain of Fire. The spider's thread thus obtained is used to wrap the body of the deceased in a true cocoon. Then the disciple need only cast the spell of Spirit Separation, transcribed in the spellbook. The disciple should take care to remain beyond reach of the cocoon in the moments that follow, for no one is permitted to witness the freeing of the soul.}
{57110}{497l The Master Weaver has allowed me to enter the Tomb of Tol Guldur. At last I will be able to discover what lies hidden there, and I will make the village peaceful once more.}
{62000}{497l Antoine,}
{62001}{497l I am preparing to cast a most powerful spell. Yes, you read that correctly, my friend. Professor Quentin Blafard, ardent defender of science and modern technology, is studying magic! The very magic I fought—or at least pretended to fight, for as you know, my wife Elisabeth is a magician... But to the point. I am willing to risk casting this spell because I cannot imagine science ever achieving such an effect. Antoine, heed me! Erwin Cornebrume was a brilliant magician! He discovered a formula for traveling back through time! At first, when I read his notes, I refused to believe it. But if this works, it will transform the entire world! I must therefore test the formula myself.
{71000}{28c
{71001}{28l
{71002}{28l Startled at first, the servants attending the sick ruler looked up and wondered who this man was and more importantly, how he had gotten past the guards. Amtut looked at the man with his deathly, sunken eyes and asked,
{71003}{28l Why, surely that is not fair sir! Surely you would prefer gold, jewels or diamonds! These things are far more vauable than heartstones! Why, you can have one hundred black diamonds if you so desire!"
{71004}{28l Amtut looked at his servants. He then looked around at his chamber before responding, "Yes. We have a deal."
{71005}{28l That is the story that I read in the warm sunlight that morning, and I would've forgotten it, if not for a strange incident that occurred one day while I was on one of my many journeys. A small village had complained about something strange happening to their sheep. Apparently, every night, the sheep would bleat constantly as if they were spooked by something. The farmers initially thought it was a local boy called 'Tim'. Tim was a prankster and used to play all sorts of jokes on the farmers by doing strange things to their sheep. That was until one night when one of the farmers decided to stay awake and see what was happening.
{71006}{28l That story was told to me by another farmer at the local inn, as I was travelling through town not more than a month later. So, being the eager adventurer I was (and still am) I headed off into the mountains in search of what I believed to be a mummy. After several days journey, I found a deep cave within the mountains and headed inside. After battling my way through several of the usual creatures, I realised that the cave was quite deeper than I had anticipated and that if I was going to get to the bottom of it, I was going to need many more supplies. I made the decision to turn around and head back to town.
{71010}{37c
{71011}{37l
{71012}{37l        Seein' as his guns were drawn I fired a shot. Bang! An' another, Bang! Down he went, Flintlock Jones never missed twice. I usually missed once, but never twice! He wasn' dead, but he was hurt pretty bad. I rifled through his gear an' made damn sure he didn't have no tricks up his sleeve (Seeing as he was a one armed Half-Orc I suppose he only had one sleeve o' tricks). Anyways, I grabbed his guns from him and put mine to 'is head.
{71013}{37l         After all that, I figured there weren't nothin' else fer me to do so I unpacked me gear an' had a bit of a stay at the hut. Nice little place, once I got the fire started it sure was cosy. The next mornin' I decided to ride back to town, although this 'ad more to do with the hut burnin' down over-night then it did with me wantin' a hero's welcome. Of course, back in town, a hero's welcome is what I got. Parade an' all! With Crazy Jimmy dead, the world was a better place.
{71020}{37l The Big Book of Quests
{71030}{37c
{71031}{37l In dialogue @pcname@ puts the PCs name in the dialogue. I want something similar for Global Variables like @gvNUM@ that will display the current value of Global Variable NUM. It would save me a whole lot of script checking when the PC asks about their bank balance in the Bank Teller dialogue. Also, I could use it for something like 'You have only killed @gv1@ rats! Go back and kill them all!' If the PC hasn't killed all the rats. While I doubt something like this would be used that often, it would give me some extra flexibility to do some fancy things for some of my quests. While you're at it, how about @gfNUM@, @pvNUM@ etc... For ALL the options, flags and variables that you can use. Again, not used that often, but it would add some extra flexibility (just in case). Also, I'd like to be able to use these same codes in the '.mes' files such as 'gamebook.mes' and 'gamenote.mes'. So that I can write a telegram that is actually addressed to the PC by using the code '@pcname@' rather than using 'adventurer'.
{71032}{37l WorldEd seems to have the unfortunate habit of saving your map AFTER you use the 'delete sector' command. This is annoying when you want make a mistake and want to go back to the version of your map BEFORE you deleted. 'Deleting' seems to have a bad habit of wiping out a sector even when you reload the map.
{71033}{37l To the individual who made the 'SockMonkey ScriptMaker'. While it was not THAT difficult working with your programme, it was however, far from pleasant. Is it possible, in a future version of ScriptMaker, to be able to edit an already existing line of script WITHOUT having to re-build the entire line? Also, goto lines should not ALWAYS remap, this was annoying because you had to not only guess the line number you wanted to 'goto', but you also had to guess what line number SockMonkey would remap your goto line to as well, if you had a line of script to delete after making the 'goto' line. I also found it quite biazarre that when I had a 'goto line Local 0' it actually changed the '0' and incremented it. When I want to go to 'Local 0', I want to go to 'Local 0', not have it remap to 'Local 1' or 'Local 2' later on when I add or delete a line of script. Although, I did find RARE occasions where remapping goto lines was appreciated. But, if it means dealing with the current situation, I'd prefer it if they didn't remap and it was instead just a lot easier to change the script.
{71034}{37l I suppose it is too late for this, but, could ALL items have an internal name by default? Currently, wine has an internal name of 'alcohol' which is good as I can use it in a beggars' dialogue. However, I have a module where I want the PC to get some 'Large Gears' and give them to an NPC. I want to be able to use ANY Large Gears. However, because 'Large Gears' does not have an internal name other than 'generic' I can not use them in a quest, instead, I have to make my own 'Large Gears' specifically for my quest and have the PC get hold of them somehow by either searching the right container or getting them from the right NPC. My intention was that the PC could buy/find ANY 'Large Gears' anywhere and use them. If EVERY item had an internal name, then it would be possible to use ANY general item in a quest (and leave me open to do some of my more ambitious ideas like never-ending quests). Keep in mind that I want EVERY item to have a unique name (in other words, 'uncut rubies' as well as 'rubies' rather than just 'rubies'. That way I can make my jeweller change uncut precious stones into cut ones and use them BOTH in quests).
{71035}{37l With all that said, I must admit that it was bloody excellent building my own module! I've gotta admit that I haven't had that much fun making a mod for a game since, well, since never :) As such, I'd like to personally thank Jason Anderson, Leonard Boyarsky, David Bragg, Timothy Cain, Mark Harrison, Chris Jones, Michael McCarthy, Chad Moore, Steve Moret, Yong Park, Jesse Reynolds, Sharon Shellman, Dominick Cecere, Michael Dean, Kurt Dekker, Edward R. G. Mortimer, Sissie Chang, Tiffany Chu, Scott Jacobson, Cynthia Komm and Sierra for publishing such a wonderful and involving game (I think that's everybody...) Arcanum truly is a game of limitless possibilities. With the editors, I have the capability to make everything from a simple hack 'n slash adventure, to a little murder mystery or even a full blown game! I don't know of another game that has that ability. Oh, and er.... If you ever need an extra pair of hands to design and create a quest, make an NPCs dialogue, figure out a script or build a town.... Could you give me a call... Please? Pretty Please? With sugar on top? And a cherry? :)
{71036}{37l Check out the Arcanum Mod Making Tutorial at:
{71040}{37l A History of Grayhills}
{71050}{37c
{71051}{37l After many years of experimentation, I believe I have devised methods with which one can ensure the long term viability of one's farm. One of these methods, crop rotation, I believe has the most beneficial advantage to the moderne farmer.
{71052}{37l In my above example, you can see that in the first year, I have planted corn and potatoes. The second year I planted wheat, followed in the third by buckwheat for green manure. In the fourth year, I again planted wheat, followed by three successive plantings of grass or clover. While the land restored itself during these plantings of grass, I used the pasture to fatten livestock. I then repeat the process for another seven year cycle. No crop, except for grasses, should be planted in the same field two years in a row.
{71053}{37l It is important to note that the crops planted must be suited to the farmers soils. It is imperative that the farmer design crop rotations to meet the nutrient needs of his soil for later crops. For crop rotations which include hay the rotation can be lengthened by maintaining the existing hay stand for additional years.
{71054}{37l
{71055}{37l Creek Mud :
{71056}{37l By combining these two methods of crop rotation and fertilizers, it is possible to increase the nutrient life of ones' fields by many years.
